    content: `<h2>How CS2 Crosshair Commands Map to Screen Pixels</h2>
<p>While Valorant standardizes everything behind compact semicolon strings, Counter-Strike 2 exposes full pixel-level control through developer console convars. Knowing the exact commands beats hunting through UI sliders—especially if you switch resolutions between <code>1280×960</code> stretched and <code>1920×1080</code> native, where negative gap values behave differently.</p>
<p>Before editing your config, you can test line proportions visually inside our <a href="/crosshair/">Crosshair Generator</a> or check verified pro player setups in the <a href="/pros/">Pro Player Settings Database</a>.</p>

<h2>The 8 Core CS2 Console Commands Every Player Needs</h2>
<ul>
  <li><code>cl_crosshairstyle 4</code> — Pure Classic Static (no movement or firing spread). Use <code>5</code> if you want subtle firing-only feedback.</li>
  <li><code>cl_crosshairsize 1.5</code> to <code>2.5</code> — Controls arm length. Most modern CS2 riflers keep length tight between <code>1.0</code> and <code>2.5</code>.</li>
  <li><code>cl_crosshairgap -3</code> to <code>-1</code> — Sets spacing from center. Negative values close the gap tightly for 1280×960 or 1080p head-taps.</li>
  <li><code>cl_crosshairthickness 0.5</code> or <code>1</code> — Sets line width; <code>0.5</code> renders cleanly on stretched 4:3, while <code>1</code> prevents disappearing pixels on 1080p/1440p.</li>
  <li><code>cl_crosshair_drawoutline 0</code> — Keeps lines crisp and minimal (<code>1</code> adds a 1px dark border controlled by <code>cl_crosshair_outlinethickness</code>).</li>
  <li><code>cl_crosshairdot 0</code> — Disables the center dot so distant heads remain unobstructed.</li>
  <li><code>cl_crosshaircolor 1</code> or <code>4</code> — <code>1</code> = Green, <code>4</code> = Cyan, or <code>5</code> for custom RGB via <code>cl_crosshaircolor_r</code>, <code>_g</code>, <code>_b</code>.</li>
  <li><code>cl_crosshair_recoil 0</code> — Disables Follow Recoil so your reticle stays anchored to true center-screen during spray transfers.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Three Pro-Style CS2 Console Presets</h2>
<p>Paste any of these three tested blocks straight into the <code>~</code> developer console (or append them to your <code>autoexec.cfg</code>) to cover the three dominant Tier-1 archetypes:</p>

<h3>1. Tight Entry Rifler (4:3 Stretched &amp; 1080p)</h3>
<p>Designed for aggressive AK-47/M4A1-S duels where you need a compact cross that never hides distant heads on Mirage Mid or Inferno Banana:</p>
<pre><code>cl_crosshairstyle 4; cl_crosshairsize 1.5; cl_crosshairgap -2.5; cl_crosshairthickness 0.5; cl_crosshair_drawoutline 0; cl_crosshairdot 0; cl_crosshaircolor 4; cl_crosshair_recoil 0; cl_crosshairalpha 255</code></pre>

<h3>2. Crisp Tap &amp; Deagle Precision (Open Center)</h3>
<p>Ideal for methodical pre-aimers who want a visible 2–3 pixel central window so enemy heads sit cleanly between the four bars:</p>
<pre><code>cl_crosshairstyle 4; cl_crosshairsize 2; cl_crosshairgap -1; cl_crosshairthickness 1; cl_crosshair_drawoutline 1; cl_crosshair_outlinethickness 1; cl_crosshairdot 0; cl_crosshaircolor 1; cl_crosshair_recoil 0</code></pre>

<h3>3. Hybrid AWPer &amp; Pistol Utility Preset</h3>
<p>Slightly larger gap with high-visibility cyan-white balance for quick unscoped knife-to-pistol switches:</p>
<pre><code>cl_crosshairstyle 4; cl_crosshairsize 2.5; cl_crosshairgap -2; cl_crosshairthickness 0.5; cl_crosshair_drawoutline 0; cl_crosshairdot 0; cl_crosshaircolor 5; cl_crosshaircolor_r 0; cl_crosshaircolor_g 255; cl_crosshaircolor_b 200; cl_crosshair_recoil 0</code></pre>

<h2>Fine-Tuning for Resolution &amp; Aspect Ratio</h2>
<p>Unlike vector UI elements, CS2 crosshairs render directly on the game's pixel grid. Moving from <code>1280×960</code> stretched to <code>1920×1080</code> native makes <code>cl_crosshairthickness 0.5</code> look razor-thin and slightly asymmetrical around the exact center pixel. If you play 1080p or 1440p native, stick to integer thickness (<code>1</code>) and adjust <code>cl_crosshairgap</code> in <code>0.5</code> steps until a USP-S or AK-47 target head fits snugly inside the gap at 25 meters. Also set <code>cl_crosshair_sniper_width 1</code> (or <code>2</code> on 1440p) if you want crisp, readable AWP scope lines.</p>
<p>In addition, verify <code>cl_crosshair_friendly_warning 1</code> so teammate hover indicators don't obscure your center pixel when stacking bombsites, and keep <code>cl_crosshairusealpha 1</code> paired with <code>cl_crosshairalpha 255</code> so thin lines never fade against bright Inferno walls or smoke bloom.</p>

<h2>Share Codes vs. <code>autoexec.cfg</code></h2>
<p>If a teammate drops a <code>CSGO-xxxxx-xxxxx-...</code> share code in chat, paste it under <em>Settings → Game → Crosshair → Share or Import</em>, and use the menu's copy button to back up your own share string before experimenting. Share codes pack every crosshair variable—including color, gap, thickness, outline, and sniper width—into one portable token that takes two seconds to swap between Faceit matches.</p>
<p>For long-term reliability, however, saving your exact <code>cl_crosshair*</code> convars inside <code>game/csgo/cfg/autoexec.cfg</code> (with <code>host_writeconfig</code> at the bottom and <code>+exec autoexec.cfg</code> in Steam launch options) guarantees every workshop map test, cloud sync hiccup, or config reset restores your exact reticle cleanly without hunting through menus. Keep separate bind aliases if you like toggling a slightly longer grenade-lineup crosshair on smoke throws before snapping back to your rifling reticle.</p>`
